{"id": "SGU_Episode_326", "title": "SGU Episode 326", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 326 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 326", "date": "October 15 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 10, "day": 15, "rogues": ["Rebecca Watson", "Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Pasteur", "quote": "\n 'Imagination should give wings to our thoughts but we always need decisive experimental proof, and when the moment comes to draw conclusions and to interpret the gathered observations, imagination must be checked and documented by the factual results of the experiment.' \n", "quotee": "\n Louis Pasteur \n", "quotee_title": "", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-326", "episode_number": 326}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "October 15: Global Handwashing Day! http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Handwashing_Day", "title": "This Day in Skepticism", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Handwashing_Day"], "title": "This Day in Skepticism"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "http://www.sciencebasedmedicine.org/index.php/vitamins-and-mortality/", "title": "Vitamins and Mortality", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.sciencebasedmedicine.org/index.php/vitamins-and-mortality/"], "title": "Vitamins and Mortality"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 4, "text": "http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-15242386", "title": "Megavirus", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-15242386"], "title": "Megavirus"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 5, "text": "http://www.theepochtimes.com/n2/science/near-death-experiences-30-years-of-research-part-1-61547.html", "title": "NDEs", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.theepochtimes.com/n2/science/near-death-experiences-30-years-of-research-part-1-61547.html"], "title": "NDEs"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 6, "text": "http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-tyne-15165928 and UFB - http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-2047746/The-proof-UFOs-exist-picture-taken-Cornish-coast.html", "title": "More UFOs", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/uk-england-tyne-15165928", "http://www.dailymail.co.uk/news/article-2047746/The-proof-UFOs-exist-picture-taken-Cornish-coast.html"], "title": "More UFOs"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 7, "text": "http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2011/10/111011163057.htm", "title": "Electrosense", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.sciencedaily.com/releases/2011/10/111011163057.htm"], "title": "Electrosense"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 8, "text": "http://skepchick.org/2011/10/the-airborne-identity/", "title": "Airborne Petition", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://skepchick.org/2011/10/the-airborne-identity/"], "title": "Airborne Petition"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 9, "text": "Answer to last week: Zaphod Beeblebrox IV", "title": "Who's That Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Who's That Noisy"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 10, "text": "http://www.sleightsofmind.com/", "title": "Interview with Stephen L. Macknik, Ph.D. and Susana Martinez-Conde, Ph.D.", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.sleightsofmind.com/"], "title": "Interview with Stephen L. Macknik, Ph.D. and Susana Martinez-Conde, Ph.D."}, "sections": []}, {"id": 11, "text": "Item #1: Astronomers discover that the intergalactic fog that was present in the early universe was likely cleared away by rogue black holes.\nItem #2: Scientists discover that communication among bacteria plays an important role in global climate change.\nItem #3: A research team has created a new form (or allotrope) of carbon that has the hardness of diamond but is amorphous.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 12, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 13, "text": "'Imagination should give wings to our thoughts but we always need decisive experimental proof, and when the moment comes to draw conclusions and to interpret the gathered observations, imagination must be checked and documented by the factual results of the experiment.' Louis Pasteur", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}]}, {"id": 14, "text": "CSIcon: http://www.centerforinquiry.net/events/csicon_2011/\nPodcast Awards: http://podcastawards.com/", "title": "Announcements", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.centerforinquiry.net/events/csicon_2011/", "http://podcastawards.com/"], "title": "Announcements"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 15, "text": "", "title": "References", "metadata": {"title": "References"}, "sections": []}]}